Takashi Iwai wrote:
> alsa-info.sh output would be helpful.  Run with --no-upload option,
> and attach the generated file.
>   

Okay, this is the plain modelless alsa-info output on a MacbookPro5,1:

http://www.alsa-project.org/db/?f=4b2f257e72523bccafd3ace1d3c7044fb5f09ff8

No sound at all.


The attached file is the alsa-info output with today's snapshot and
model=MB5.

* Sound is working good, the quality is much better.
* Microphone is working,
* Front channel controls the headphone but is not muted when a headphone
is inserted.

I think we could just add the SSID to the MB5 model with or without
solving the HP sensing stuff.

Thanks,
Ozan Caglayan



